{"id":"faculty-ruhul_amin:e0010","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Brief Profile :","bbox":null,"level":4,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"faculty-ruhul_amin:e0011","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Dr. Ruhul Amin is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Computer Science and Engineering Discipline. Prior to joining IIIT Naya Raipur, he was an assistant professor of NIT Jamshedpur. Dr. Amin received doctoral (Ph.D.) degree in Computer Science and Engineering from the Indian Institute of Technology(ISM) Dhanbad, Jharkhand, India, in 2017 and received B.Tech and M.Tech both in Computer Science and Engineering from Maulana Abul Kalam Azad University of Technology, West Bengal, India in 2009 and 2013, respectively. He has authored many technical research papers published in leading international conferences and peer-reviewed international journals from the IEEE, Elsevier, Springer, John Wiley, etc. He is an Associate Editor of “Security and Privacy” and \"Security and communication networks\" published by John Wiley and Hindwai respectively. He is an active senior member of IEEE and a member of ACM.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"faculty-ruhul_amin:e0012","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"In 2021, Stanford University has released a list that represents the top 2 per cent of the most-cited scientists in various disciplines. In recognition of exceptional research performance demonstrated by production of multiple highly cited papers, Dr. Amin made it to the list of Top 2% of the most cited scientists released by the US-based prestigious standford university.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
